-- Playbook database-correction.invoice-cancellation1.2.0; shared PBR01..06/PAR01..07 apply.
-- Canonical guide: ../../invoice-receipt-correction/references/sql-contracts.md
-- Generate complete original-row standby DML recovery from the current action's immutable before-snapshot.
-- Restore every deleted charge transaction/QR/mapping/invoice row using captured columns/nulls/timestamps,
-- in the real dependency order (transaction/QR parents before dependent mapping/invoice rows where needed).
-- For transaction-only follow-up restore only that action's deleted charges; do not recreate invoices/QRs
-- canceled by an earlier committed action. Never reconstruct accounting, clear history or invent columns.
-- Guard database/SID/entity, exact ID/period/count sets and ACTUAL COMMITTED full after-state/bindings.
-- Reject PK/reference/period conflicts, schema/reference-inventory drift, changed retained rows/settings
-- and new receipt/bank/payment evidence. No ON CONFLICT overwrite or production backup-table DDL.
-- Assert each actual restore count and exact original transaction/collection/balance/full snapshot afterward.
-- Default ROLLBACK; a later live restore requires fresh exact-action approval. Automatic rollback of an
-- uncommitted failed action is immediate and is not this separately gated postcommit recovery procedure.
BEGIN;
DO $authoring_only$ BEGIN
  RAISE EXCEPTION 'AUTHORING_TEMPLATE_ONLY: author full deleted-charge/invoice/QR/mapping recovery and bind actual committed after-state';
END $authoring_only$;
ROLLBACK;
